================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY LICENSES
================================================================================

The Muffin / Goo-Goo / Visu / Pip firmware links against several third-party
libraries with their own license terms. The MIT terms above apply ONLY to the
source code in this repository. Binaries distributed by downstream users may
be subject to additional license obligations from these dependencies:

  Library                   | License        | Notes
  --------------------------|----------------|------------------------------
  m5stack/M5Unified         | MIT            | hardware abstraction
  m5stack/M5GFX             | MIT            | display library (via M5Unified)
  m5stack/M5Module-LLM      | MIT            | LLM module bridge (cores3 only)
  bblanchon/ArduinoJson     | MIT            | JSON parsing
  espressif/arduino-esp32   | LGPL 2.1 + MIT | framework
  schreibfaul1/ESP32-audioI2S | GPL v3.0    | MP3 stream decoder (web radio)

The web radio feature pulls in `ESP32-audioI2S`, which is licensed under
GPL v3.0. That is a strong copyleft license: any binary that statically
links against it inherits the GPL v3.0 distribution terms. Concretely this
means:

  * `cores3`, `core2`, `visu` envs DO link the audio library — binaries
    built from those envs are practical-purposes governed by GPL v3.0 when
    redistributed.
  * `pip` env does NOT link the audio library (no web radio on Pip) — its
    binary can be redistributed under MIT terms only.
  * The source code in this repository remains MIT regardless of which env
    you build.

If you want a fully-MIT binary distribution and don't need web radio, drop
`ESP32-audioI2S` from `lib_deps_wifi` in `platformio.ini` and stub out
`webradio.cpp`.
